(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-01","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["第三声铜钟敲响时，沈砚在大殿后排站直了，没有随众人跪拜。十七名等候考核的[[disciple|弟子]]中，只有他的袖口沾着干泥。清晨他蹲了半个时辰，药田的青灵草已卷起枯边，连母亲留下的银扣也失去了[[spiritual|灵性的]]微光。韩长老宣布，十二日后将举行公开[[trial|审判]]，裁定无主药田的归属。沈砚举起旧契：人还站在这里，怎么就成了无主田？掌簿执事伸手，向他索要续期的[[proof|证据]]。","契纸上留着母亲的[[signature|签名]]，下角却被茶水洇掉两行。执事说，缺少续期的[[clause|条款]]，旧契便不足为凭。韩长老敲了敲案几，交给沈砚一项[[assignment|任务]]：十日内查明南坡断流的缘由，带回旧账，才准他在审判前申辩；逾期便逐出山门。南坡早已缺水，长老为何等药田枯死才问？沈砚压下这句话，先逼执事盖好下山的[[permit|许可证]]，才在任务文书上按下指印。","转身欲走时，顾衡横剑拦在阶前。这个[[formidable|难以对付的]]师兄曾几次阻住他的考核，今日右腕却在发抖，宽袖试图[[conceal|隐藏]]一圈新缠的厚布。顾衡问他，一张破纸也配改变命数？沈砚只说，师兄的手正在流血。那张冷脸顿时绷紧。顾衡又拿药田刺他，想[[provoke|激怒]]他，好让执事收回通行文书。沈砚凭着多年受挫练出的[[restraint|克制]]，避开剑鞘，收脚让了半步。","他没有立刻出门，而是回到案前，要求查看南坡的修渠记录。要[[investigate|调查]]断水，先得知道谁动过闸。图上没有改渠的记载，泥样里却混着新铁锈，这道[[trace|痕迹]]使他当众说出了自己的[[suspicion|怀疑]]：泉水未必干了，也可能被截去了别处。管事避开他的目光。韩长老喝止议论，沈砚收起泥包，没有把尚未查清的[[motive|动机]]说成定案。他只请执事记下今日的问话，免得十日后又有人说从没人提过。","出了山门，年轻医者罗清拦住他，问能否借半壶净水。她刚给五个喝过黑沙水的孩子看诊。沈砚分出水，随她去失踪守渠人周伯的小屋，门锁着，窗下却有湿鞋。两人沿渠壁找到一块刻着[[inscription|碑文]]的[[ancient|古老的]]石板：山取一份，谷取两份。银扣的缺口恰好合上一旁的凹槽。沈砚在灯下[[discern|辨认]]出新涂的灰浆——那个二被改成了零。十日任务的[[deadline|截止期限]]还在逼近，他要查的却已不只是自家的药田。"],"en":["When the third bronze bell rang, Shen Yan straightened at the back of the hall instead of kneeling. Of the seventeen [[disciple|disciples]] awaiting assessment, only he had dry mud on his sleeves. He had crouched in his field for half an hour that morning. The herb leaves were curling, and even his mother's silver clasp had lost its faint [[spiritual|spiritual]] glow. Elder Han announced a public [[trial|trial]] in twelve days to decide who owned unclaimed herb fields. Shen raised his old deed. How could his field be unclaimed while he was standing there? The clerk held out a hand and demanded [[proof|proof]] of renewal.","His mother's [[signature|signature]] remained on the deed, but tea had blurred two lines at the bottom. The clerk said the missing renewal [[clause|clause]] made it insufficient. Han tapped the table and gave Shen an [[assignment|assignment]]: discover why the southern channel had run dry and bring back its old accounts within ten days. Only then could he present his case before the hearing. Failure meant expulsion. The slope had lacked water for some time. Why ask now, after the herbs had withered? Shen held back that question. He made the clerk stamp his travel [[permit|permit]] before pressing a fingerprint onto the task document.","As Shen turned to leave, Gu Heng barred the steps with his sword. The [[formidable|formidable]] senior had repeatedly blocked Shen's assessments, but today his right wrist trembled. His broad sleeve could not quite [[conceal|conceal]] its fresh bandage. Gu asked whether a scrap of paper deserved to change anyone's fate. Shen merely said his hand was bleeding. Gu's face tightened. He taunted Shen about the field again, hoping to [[provoke|provoke]] an outburst that would let the clerk withdraw the travel papers. Drawing on the [[restraint|restraint]] he had learned through years of setbacks, Shen avoided the scabbard and stepped aside.","Instead of leaving immediately, Shen returned to the desk and requested the channel maintenance records. To [[investigate|investigate]] the shortage, he first needed to know who had touched the gate. The drawing showed no alterations, yet his mud sample contained fresh iron rust. This [[trace|trace]] prompted him to voice his [[suspicion|suspicion]]: the spring might not have dried up; someone might have diverted it. The steward avoided his eyes. Han silenced the murmurs. Shen put away the sample without treating an unproven [[motive|motive]] as a verdict. He asked only that his questions be recorded, so nobody could deny them ten days later.","Outside, Luo Qing, a young healer, stopped him to ask for half a flask of clean water. She had just treated five children who had drunk water full of black sand. Shen shared his water and followed her to the cottage of Zhou, the missing channel keeper. Its door was locked, but wet shoes stood under the window. Along the channel wall they found an [[ancient|ancient]] stone bearing an [[inscription|inscription]]: one share for the mountain, two for the valley. The notch in the silver clasp fitted a groove beside it. In the lamplight Shen could [[discern|discern]] fresh plaster. Someone had changed the two to a zero. His ten-day [[deadline|deadline]] was approaching, but the inquiry now concerned more than his own field."]});
